{%- comment -%}
  Objection-handling / comparison content page — the kind of page a
  competitor's site (Brick Me) runs against the official LEGO Mosaic
  Maker. Deliberately does NOT put specific numeric claims about a named
  competitor's color count, pricing or sizes in this file: those facts
  aren't verifiable from inside this codebase and would need the merchant
  to confirm current, accurate figures before publishing — getting a
  competitor comparison factually wrong is worse than not publishing one.
  What IS safely claimed here is MemoBrick's own, already-verified numbers
  (used elsewhere on this site) and its real review base.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- render 'site-header' -%}
<script type="application/ld+json">
{
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "BreadcrumbList",
  "itemListElement": [
    { "@type": "ListItem", "position": 1, "name": "MemoBrick", "item": {{ request.origin | append: '/' | json }} },
    { "@type": "ListItem", "position": 2, "name": "Custom brick mosaics, compared", "item": {{ canonical_url | json }} }
  ]
}
</script>
<div class="wrap" style="padding:48px 20px 90px;max-width:820px">
  <p style="font-family:var(--mono);font-size:11px;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--ink-3)">
    <a href="/" style="color:inherit;text-decoration:none">MemoBrick</a> <span aria-hidden="true">›</span> Custom brick mosaics, compared
  </p>
  <h1 style="font-family:var(--display);font-size:32px;letter-spacing:-.03em;margin:10px 0 8px">
    Turning a photo into brick art: what actually matters.
  </h1>
  <p style="color:var(--ink-2);font-size:16px;max-width:640px;margin:0 0 40px">
    There's more than one way to turn a photo into a brick mosaic — an official mosaic maker, a generic
    third-party kit, or MemoBrick's own proof-before-production process. Here's what to actually weigh.
  </p>

  <div style="display:grid;gap:28px">
    <article>
      <h2 style="font-family:var(--display);font-size:19px;margin:0 0 6px">You see it before it's made</h2>
      <p style="color:var(--ink-2);line-height:1.6">Every MemoBrick order gets a real proof — a preview of your
        exact photo, at your exact size, before anything ships. Not every mosaic tool does this; some just
        hand you instructions and hope the result matches what you imagined.</p>
    </article>
    <article>
      <h2 style="font-family:var(--display);font-size:19px;margin:0 0 6px">Faces are handled specifically</h2>
      <p style="color:var(--ink-2);line-height:1.6">Skin tones, shadows and small facial details are the hardest
        part of any photo mosaic — most tools treat a face like any other patch of color. MemoBrick's Creator
        analyzes faces specifically and protects them through the color-matching process, and recommends a
        larger size automatically when a photo has more detail than a small board can hold.</p>
    </article>
    <article>
      <h2 style="font-family:var(--display);font-size:19px;margin:0 0 6px">Real reviews, real photos</h2>
      <p style="color:var(--ink-2);line-height:1.6">MemoBrick has 747 customer reviews, most with a photo of
        the finished piece — pet memorials, wedding photos, family portraits, gifts for people going through
        something hard. <a href="/pages/happy-customers" style="color:var(--b-red);font-weight:600">Read them
        here</a> before you decide.</p>
    </article>
    <article>
      <h2 style="font-family:var(--display);font-size:19px;margin:0 0 6px">Help when you want it, hands-off when you don't</h2>
      <p style="color:var(--ink-2);line-height:1.6">Design it yourself in the free Creator, or hand your photo to
        MemoBrick's designers and get a proof to approve — both paths ship the same kit, the same instructions,
        and the same 2–4 business day dispatch from Miami, FL.</p>
    </article>
  </div>

  <p style="margin-top:44px">
    <a class="btn btn-red" href="/pages/editor">Design your MemoBrick</a>
  </p>
</div>

